of "one of the most distinguished and honoured men England has
ever produced; in whose loss every man among us feels that he
has lost a friend and an instructor." Temple-Hatton, 10th of June
1870.</p></div>
<div class="footnote"><p><a id="Footnote_239_239"></a><a href="#FNanchor_239_239" class="pginternal"><span class="label">[239]</span></a> If space were available here, his letters would supply many proofs
